WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.870 align:start position:0%
 
it's not out of fashion  to put on a bulletproof jacket and a  ballistic helmet  it was an effort to secure my life  some more that is after i survived  gun attacks more than once more than  twice  i was targeted my car was riddled with  bullets flattening all tyres  and that one occasion the military shoot  into the windscreen of my car  miraculously i'm still alive and nobody  was shot dead  in my car however many of my close  allies have been shot dead  i have been targeted uh by tiago's  canisters  and life bullets every single person  that i've been moving with on the  campaign trail has been  partner has been hit from producer dan  magic who was hit by  with the tiago's canister splitting his  face to my close  ally and singing partner nobian lee was  shot on the head  to my personal security  who was targeted and shot on the eye and  a few days ago  my close journalist who was covering the  events around me  in the campaign trail who showed  directly in the head  smashing his skull and  part of his brain was exposed so  wearing a ballistic helmet and a  bulletproof vest  is an effort to secure my life the  election  is being stolen and rigged not will be  by the mere fact that i was arrested on  the day of nomination that have been  blocked from campaigns that my posters  are not allowed to be there that i'm not  allowed to have any billboards  that i'm blocked from radio and tv  stations that i'm a candidate  a presidential candidate who is not  allowed to drive on main roads  or to even to address people in towns  that's a rig but the mere fact that the  electoral commission has come out to  block me  just me from campaigning in more than 30  districts  and indeed the electoral commission said  i must sign a memorandum of  understanding with them  before they can allow me to proceed  campaigning while everybody else is  campaigning  by pretending to ban campaigns in  the most populated areas where we have  more than 45 percent of the voters  and yet genome 70 the incumbent  president continues to campaign  under the protection of police and  military by the harassment that  has been ongoing the mass murder that  has been carried out  by the police and the military by the  habitual arrest of 100  of my campaign team on the 30th of  november in kalangala island  and myself inclusive only that i was  seeing  singularity airlifted by the military  and  dumped and detained in my house by the  fact that  even when i came up with another  campaign team it was all rounded up  yesterday and arrested  that proves that the ground is not  leveled there's no free unfair fairness  freedom and fairness here  however we are going into this election  as a protest i have been calling upon  ugandans to come out  and vote this is our only opportunity we  are non-violent  so we're using this election as a  protest  to speak and speak loudly  the election is being stolen because the  military and the police  have taken over the duty of the  electoral commission  it is not the electoral commission that  is in charge it is the military  people are not allowed to use their  phones and cameras to record the  proceedings  the electoral commission just came out  recently and banned  journalists from covering the elections  this comes at the backdrop of  deporting very many  international journalists that had come  to cover the election  it comes at the backdrop of the european  union  being unable to come and uh watch this  election  however we know that we are 45 million  ugandans  and we ensured that we call upon people  to register massively we have  18 million voters when all these people  come out  and vote we are sure they will be able  to assert their voices  and that will change our country forever  we are going to get our freedom or we  shall die trying to get our freedom  good enough we are non-violent and we  are living in a generation where the  world is watching  our biggest weapon is the camera  exposing all the atrocities that are  being committed against the people of  uganda  yesterday i announced to the  international community  and to the world that we are petitioning  the international criminal court  to investigate genome 70 general elite  mini and  all these other security bosses  over the crimes against humanity that  continue  to be committed against the people of  uganda we know that all these efforts  will bear fruit one day  i live every day as if it's the last day  my life is threatened my the life of my  wife is threatened  my close allies and everybody that  associates with me  but we keep going knowing that our lives  do not end with us so many people have  already paid the ultimate price  and my life is not any much more  valuable than the lives of the people of  uganda  of course like anybody else i love  to live a long life but there comes a  time  when life is only life when it's lived  freely the united kingdom  and uganda have very close ties  we have historical ties but i also want  to believe that what binds us together  are the values that we share as the two  nations  values like the rule of law values like  respect to  human rights values like respect  and governing according to the  principles of democracy  these are values that we have called  upon all development partners  all allies of uganda regionally  continentally and internationally  to push our leaders to to remember that  they are not dealing with museveni  they're individual they're dealing with  merced  on the on behalf of the people of uganda  he's  76 also he says although we believe he's  much older  he's not going to live forever  we always appeal to them to  have their collaboration their  cooperation with the people of uganda  not most having as an individual and to  always  stand by the values that they profess  we always ask them to make a  precondition of  respect for democratic principles  respect for human rights and respect for  the rule of law  to make them preconditions for  cooperation with uganda  what we want to achieve from the  international criminal court first and  foremost is to send a message  to genome 70 that he is not above the  law that in the year 2021  no body can commit crimes against  humanity  and get away with it we want  those investigations and the findings  to hold the genome seven accountable  we are aware that there are plans  to commit mass crimes to commit mass  violence  there's a plan to kill so many people by  the military  and the police we want to send a message  to general mustafini  that the world is watching and for every  single crime that he commits  against humanity there will be  a day of recon there will be a day when  he will have to  answer for those crimes and to also send  a message  to all those that hold guns to know that  in this time and era no human being  must be subjected to human rights abuses  and to also send the message to the  dictators  all over the world that they  may take long to fall but they  eventually fall  one by one the uganda  we want to live in what we call a new  uganda  is a uganda where  there is sovereign leadership there's a  uganda  where the government is a  people-centered government a uganda  where everybody is equal before and  under  the law in uganda where the law protects  us the same  and punish us the same in uganda  where there's equal opportunity  for everybody equal access to employment  equal access to  quality education and quality health  care  for every ugandan regardless of their  second name or where  they come from or who they know in  uganda  where you know there's equitable  balanced um economic  development for everybody  where we don't just see those  in positions of authority throwing  around statistics  to explain economic growth but in real  sense  the masses the bulk of the population is  languishing  is suffering is sweating under the yoke  of poverty  you want to live in a uganda where  people  are not evicted from their land  by the rich and mighty in the armed  forces and in government  in uganda where um  want to live in uganda where um  [Music]  there is equal rights and justice where  then  the the um  natural resources of the country belong  to the citizens  not where you see the president saying  it's my oil  where the president  is having a brother that has taken over  all the gold in muvende  in uganda where the president gives  the gold and the natural resources and  the minerals of a certain region  to the wife as a  birthday gift we want to live in uganda  where the natural resources of the  country  benefit the citizens in uganda  where we are no longer a laughingstock  among nations  uganda that has healthy relations  with our neighbors with sister countries  where we don't have  to have borders closed on us in uganda  where we  are respected and upload on the  international platform  and not being known for poverty  for disease for corruption and for  dictatorship that's a uganda that i  envision that we envision  as a generation

